---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, href } from "../data/site";
---
<Base title="About" description="What the ORCHESTRA is, the domain it serves, and the disciplines that make its outputs trustworthy." path="/about">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>An orchestra for causal decision support</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">Scientific analytics increasingly chain a fitted model to an automated
        decision, and the danger is silent: a model that fits an outcome well can still encode a
        confounded or unverified association, and a naive calibrate-then-optimise pipeline will act
        on it.</p>
      <p class="mt-2">The orchestra's answer is composition under discipline. Single-responsibility
        packages meet at one versioned result contract; a contract-typed engine performs the plan.
        Two disciplines are load-bearing. <strong>Calibrated abstention</strong>: the system refuses to
        issue a decision when the evidence is under-powered, the lenses disagree, or an input is
        unverified. And the <strong>Independent Oracle Principle</strong>: every fact about an external
        authority is grounded against a reference the system did not produce, and an ungrounded fact
        is refused rather than acted on.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Domain</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">{site.domain}. Grain production is the application anchor — a method that cannot
        be exemplified on a real grain-production decision is parked, not pursued. All data is
        publication-friendly surrogate (public agricultural-trial datasets and simulators); no
        restricted field data enters any package.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">How this site was built</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Every member name, capability, contract, count, and number on this site was
        grounded against the orchestra's own source of truth before it was shown; where a fact could
        not be verified, it was left out or marked open. The frontier tools were checked against their
        official sources. The site holds itself to the same standard the orchestra holds its science.</p>

      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/members")}>The catalogue</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/")}>The constellation</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
